The producer descriptor becomes the terminal child's stdin, stdout and
stderr, and it is opened with O_NONBLOCK. Nothing clears the flag before
the child is executed, so children start with non-blocking stdio and reads
that would block fail with EAGAIN instead, which nothing expects from a
tty: a shell read loop treats the error as end of input and exits at once,
cat exits without reading anything, and zellij panics out of its stdin
thread. Programs that reset the flag themselves hide the problem, so a
long lived session can look healthy while a fresh one dies during startup.

Open the producer blocking instead. kitty drives the other end of the pty,
which is unaffected.

